    "blurb": "Execute Nextcloud operations from Camunda",
    "overview": "The Nextcloud File connector runs file and folder operations in Nextcloud directly from Camunda BPMN processes. Create and list folders, and upload, download, copy, move, and delete files, without additional service implementation or custom backend logic.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Execute file and folder operations in Nextcloud from Camunda",
    "splashDescription": "The Nextcloud File connector for Camunda is a custom connector that enables file and folder operations in Nextcloud to be executed directly from Camunda BPMN processes. Using Nextcloud’s standardized WebDAV API, the connector integrates directly into existing process models, without the need for additional service implementation or custom backend logic. This allows companies to fully automate document-based processes, such as for archiving, document routing, reporting, or file synchronization. The connector is suitable for both SaaS and Self-Managed environments and supports modern security and deployment standards. It enables the integration of Camunda processes with Nextcloud-based file management, directly modelable in BPMN. Disclaimer: Nextcloud is a trademark of Nextcloud GmbH. This connector is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nextcloud.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/873772/overview/img9160577022482418381.png?efd3d563cb012d1bdc6065d018ffe8c4",
